  <h2>1. Product scope</h2>
  <p>
    AgentOS provides real-estate workflow software (CRM, leads, listings,
    marketing tools, seller intake, professional networking) and a non-MLS
    public marketplace for listings intentionally published by authorized users
    or supported data providers (RentCast, Untera, RealtyAPI). MLS/IDX/CPAR/Trestle
    connectivity is not part of the current launch and would require separate
    authorization.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Accounts, Professionals, Buyers, and Sellers</h2>
  <p>
    You must provide accurate information to create an account and are
    responsible for activity under your account and for protecting your
    credentials. Professionals remain solely responsible for their own
    real-estate licensing, authorization, property accuracy, advertising
    compliance, consumer consent, communications compliance, and applicable law.
    AgentOS is not an appraisal service, MLS, brokerage, law firm, lender, or
    financial adviser, and does not verify every claim a Professional or Seller
    makes about a property.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Marketplace and listing information</h2>
  <p>
    Only records explicitly eligible for public publication may appear in the
    public marketplace. Seller submissions require Professional review before
    publication. Listings sourced from RentCast, Untera, or RealtyAPI are shown
    as supplied by those providers, with attribution; AgentOS does not
    independently verify third-party listing data and is not responsible for its
    accuracy. Report suspected misuse through the AgentOS abuse channel.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Subscriptions, credits, and billing</h2>
  <p>
    Paid plans and credit purchases are billed through Paddle.com, which acts as
    Merchant of Record for the transaction, applicable tax, buyer billing
    support, and eligible returns or refunds. Custom credit purchases require a
    minimum amount, shown at checkout. Credits and paid features are made
    available only after payment is confirmed by Paddle; AgentOS does not grant
    paid access on an unconfirmed or pending payment. See the
    <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a> and <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a> page
    for details. You can manage or cancel a subscription from your account
    billing settings.
  </p>

